Package: confoundvis
Type: Package
Title: A Common Interface for Visualizing and Reporting Sensitivity
    Analyses for Unmeasured Confounding
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "Subir",
      family = "Hait",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "haitsubi@msu.edu",
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-9871-9677")
    )
Description: A common interface to established sensitivity analyses for
    unmeasured confounding in observational studies. Results of impact
    threshold and robustness of inference to replacement analysis (Frank,
    2000, <doi:10.1177/0049124100029002001>; Frank et al., 2013,
    <doi:10.3102/0162373713493129>), partial R-squared omitted-variable bias
    analysis (Cinelli and Hazlett, 2020, <doi:10.1111/rssb.12348>), E-values
    (VanderWeele and Ding, 2017, <doi:10.7326/M16-2607>), and Rosenbaum
    bounds for matched pairs (Rosenbaum, 2002,
    <doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-3692-2>) are stored in one object that keeps
    each framework's own parameter. Robustness curves, summary tables,
    and plain-language reports are available for every framework;
    two-parameter surfaces, the exact correlation contour, and
    observed-covariate benchmarks are provided where the corresponding
    framework defines them. Results
    can be computed from fitted models or matched-pair differences, or
    converted from the 'sensemakr', 'konfound', and 'EValue' packages, and
    agree with those packages.
